## Behavior 1 — output lane name lifted below the bus, clear of the seams (#76)

Gate: `src/ui/smoke.test.tsx` → describe "Schematic" → it "puts output lane
names below the bus, clear of the seams (#76)". The test reads the restored
layout's real geometry (`computeLayout(workedResult(), 20)`): output
`track.busY = 176`, seam band `busY ± 6` = [170, 182], lifted output name
baseline `busY + 18 = 194`. It pins the SVG `class="lane-name" x="4" y="194"`
and the geometry gate `nameBandTop (194−11=183) > seamBandBottom (182)` — the
~1px clearance.

- PASS at HEAD: `Tests  1 passed | 60 skipped (61)`.
- BREAK: in `Schematic.tsx`, revert the output lift back to the garble baseline —
  `y={side === "output" ? track.busY + 18 : track.y + 12}` → `y={track.y + 12}`.
- FAIL observed:
  > `× puts output lane names below the bus, clear of the seams (#76)`
  > `AssertionError: expected '<div class="schematic">…' to contain 'class="lane-name" x="4" y="194"'`
  > `Received: … <text class="lane-name" x="4" y="180">Iron Ingot</text> …`
  (with the lift removed the output name renders at y="180" = track.y+12, NOT the
  lifted y="194"; the seam-clearance geometry pin would also break since the name
  band would then straddle the bus.)
- RESTORE + green: `Tests  1 passed | 60 skipped (61)`.

## Behavior 2 — Combined view removed, compile-gated (#75)

Gate: the deletion of `chainConnectors` / `chainTransportPower` /
`ChainConnector` / `ChainPowerFooter` / `isVehicleModeLink` / `deriveChainView`
from the codebase. Any live reference to a deleted export fails `tsc -b` (the
`check` command's first stage). This is the true gate — the removal is enforced
by the type checker, not by a string sweep.

- PASS at HEAD: `npm run check` clean (`tsc -b && eslint . && prettier --check`).
- BREAK: re-add `chainConnectors` to the import list in `chain-view.test.ts`.
- FAIL observed:
  > `src/ui/chain-view.test.ts(18,3): error TS2305: Module '"./chain-view.ts"' has no exported member 'chainConnectors'.`
  > `src/ui/chain-view.test.ts(18,3): error TS6133: 'chainConnectors' is declared but its value is never read.`
- RESTORE + green: `tsc -b` clean.

Supporting: the App boot test's `not.toContain("chain-bp")` / `not.toContain(
"COMBINED")` guards the initializing SSR surface. NOTE (honest scope): App SSR
renders only `<p class="boot">Loading…</p>` in node (catalog "initializing"), so
the solved block + view tabs are NOT SSR-reachable — verified by dumping the SSR
markup. The tab-default + active-marking is therefore a browser-walk gate (as the
contract states: "SSR markup if reachable; otherwise pin the tabs' presence …").
The compile gate above is the enforceable removal proof.

