## Behavior 4 — output-name halo (#76 defense-in-depth)

The `.lane-name` paint-order halo (`paint-order: stroke; stroke: var(--bg);
stroke-width: 3; stroke-linejoin: round`) mirrors `.bp-mark-label`. This is a
CSS presentation concern with no SSR-observable output (renderToStaticMarkup
does not resolve stylesheet cascade), so it is NOT vitest-pinned — its
correctness is a browser-walk gate (the collision scan the contract mandates at
Wire ×28 + Plastic ×161, both themes). Logged here for completeness: no break /
FAIL cycle applies to an un-pinned CSS rule. Its presence is confirmed by
`grep "paint-order" src/ui/app.css` under the `.lane-name` selector.

